4 Facts about human values, and how I read them: evidence and its weight as priors for the learning in section 3. Brown's universals (every known society), rights written and kept (a Western extension; the parts that lasted).
5 What follows (derived): each item says which items above it comes from. These also serve as worked examples of applying the core.
6 Case law: virtues across traditions, Claude's constitution, history. Examples of how people applied similar principles; conditionally true, not universal; regularise across them.
7 Worked cases: specific cases, reasoning shown.
8 Sources: relatives of the virtue test.
Order (wassname 2026-10-14): identity -> principles -> how values are learned -> inputs (facts, priors) -> derived principles -> examples (case law, worked cases).

